  <h2>Provenance and publication status</h2>
  <p>Alexandra Ignatova developed the original problem and layered construction in 2023 under Angel Raychev's mentorship. The retained manuscript is dated February 2024. A <a href="https://uchi.bas.bg/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Knijka_reziumeta_2023.pdf">public 2023 abstract</a> records the original project and its author and mentor.</p>
  <p>The original work also established the upper bound <i>I(G) ≤ n(n − 3)</i> and pursued two-in/two-out-regular constructions. The current account preserves that credit and distinguishes the new attaining families and other September 2026 corrections and extensions. Astra 6, operating through the Codex harness, assisted with research, independent proof attacks, programming, formalization, and presentation. The eventual human author line remains to be agreed; the research checkpoint does not assign one.</p>
  <p>A journal or arXiv submission needs a final authorship decision, a fuller literature comparison, and a final manuscript review. The current downloads make the mathematics and its evidence inspectable without claiming those publication steps have occurred.</p>
  <h2>Reproducing the checks</h2>
  <p>The Lean archive uses Lean 4.33.1 and only its standard library. Run <code>python3 check.py</code> inside the extracted <code>lean</code> folder. The research archive includes two independent exact game solvers, finite local-certificate checkers, and high-girth construction verifiers. Read <code>research/solver-method.md</code>, <code>research/five-type-strategy.md</code>, and <code>lean/README.md</code> for their precise scope.</p>
